            "text": "### 1. Commercial Viability Assessment\n\n#### Candidate A\n* **Player Perception:** Prototype. \n* **Visual Reasons:** While cleaner than B, the HUD relies on generic, unstyled thin health bars, default sans-serif system fonts, and standard asset-store iconography. The elements lack borders, unique textures, and diegetic polish expected in a commercial release.\n* **Verdict:** Prototype\n\n#### Candidate B\n* **Player Perception:** Prototype.\n* **Visual Reasons:** Heavy presence of raw debug-style plain text dumps in the upper left, center, and lower right margins. The stat bars are blocky, unstyled solid rectangles, and the ability binds look like placeholder developer readouts rather than finished graphic elements.\n* **Verdict:** Prototype\n\n---\n\n### 2. Quantitative Evaluation\n*(Scores compressed to a 3\u20137 range per instructions)*\n\n| Metric | Candidate A | Candidate B |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: |\n| **HUD Professionalism** | 5 / 10 | 3 / 10 |\n| **Scene Coherence** | 5 / 10 | 4 / 10 |\n| **Visual Identity** | 4 / 10 | 3 / 10 |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Ranking and Recommendations\n\n**Rank:**\n1. **Candidate A**\n2. **Candidate B**\n\n#### Primary Improvements\n* **Candidate A:** Introduce bespoke frame art, textured materials, and stylized typography to the gauges and hotbar to replace the minimalist placeholder aesthetic and reinforce the frontier science-fantasy theme.\n* **Candidate B:** Strip out all raw developer debug text strings from the screen edges and replace the oversized flat bars with an integrated, stylized HUD frame.",
